# Foreword

This Rulebook sets out the rules and requirements that all participating teams and players must observe when taking part in the 5EPlay Professional Challenge Season 1 (hereinafter "5EPC S1 2026" or "the Tournament"). Its purpose is to guarantee fair competition, promote the spirit of sportsmanship, and safeguard the integrity of the Tournament. Any breach of this Rulebook may lead to the penalties described herein.

By registering for or participating in the Tournament, players, substitutes, coaches, team managers and other accompanying personnel are deemed to have read, understood and agreed to be bound by all provisions of this Rulebook.

The Tournament Administration holds the final decision on all matters concerning the Tournament. For exceptional circumstances not expressly covered by this Rulebook, or where necessary to protect competitive fairness and Tournament integrity, the Tournament Administration may issue supplementary rulings in a fair and impartial manner and may, in exceptional cases, depart from the literal wording of these rules. All rulings of the Tournament Administration on disputes are final, and repeated submissions on the same matter will not be accepted.

5EPlay is committed to delivering high-quality, fair, exciting and mutually respectful esports competition for players, viewers and partners. We thank all participating teams for taking part.

