## 3. Stage Format Overview

**Open Qualifiers (online):** open registration on a first-come, first-served basis. The qualifiers are divided into 4 groups played as single round-robins, with 6 teams per group; every match is a Best of 1 (BO1). The top 2 teams of each group advance to the Group Stage, for 8 teams in total. Qualifier teams and directly invited teams enter the Tournament at the same stage (the Group Stage).

**Group Stage / Main Event (online):** 16 teams compete under the Swiss (Swiss System) format. Rounds 1 and 2 are BO1, while advancement and elimination rounds are BO3. A team advances to the Playoffs upon accumulating 3 wins and is eliminated upon accumulating 3 losses; 8 teams in total advance. All directly invited teams start at the same stage; higher-VRS teams receive no delayed entry and no bye.

**Playoffs (online):** 8 teams compete in a Single Elimination bracket. Every match is a Best of 3 (BO3) except the Grand Final, which is a Best of 5 (BO5).

